.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-UPLOAD-FILE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-upload-file \- upload a local file to a bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm upload-file
.BR \-\-bucket\-ern | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.BR \-\-file | \-f
.I PATH
[\fB\-\-part\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-concurrency\fR|\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uploads a local file to a bucket. This is the only upload action
exposed by
.BR euclid-cli (1).
Files smaller than
.B \-\-part\-size
are stored in a single request; larger files are transparently split
into parts and uploaded via the create-upload/upload-part/
complete-upload sequence behind the scenes, so multipart upload is
invisible to the caller either way.
.PP
The file is read from disk sequentially, but up to
.B \-\-concurrency
parts are uploaded in parallel in background threads, so network
latency for one part overlaps with reading and uploading the next.
Each part is retried a few times with backoff on network failures or a
server error (HTTP 5xx) before the whole upload is aborted; a rejected
part (HTTP 4xx) is not retried.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the destination bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Destination key (path) within the bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Local file to upload. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-part\-size " " \fIBYTES\fR
Size of each part, in bytes. Defaults to \fI5242880\fR (5 MiB), or the
value of \fIeuclid.modules.esm.part-size\fR in the loaded
configuration file if set - see
.BR \-\-config
in
.BR euclid-cli (1).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-concurrency " " \fIN\fR
Number of parts to upload in parallel. Defaults to \fI4\fR, or the
value of \fIeuclid.modules.esm.concurrency\fR in the loaded
configuration file if set; values less than \fI1\fR are treated as
\fI1\fR.
.PP
The bucket may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was uploaded; the completed object's metadata is printed as
JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the local file could not be opened or
stat'd, no bucket with that ERN exists, or any part failed to upload
after retries.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm upload-file \e
    --bucket-ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --key 2026-08.csv --file ./2026-08.csv

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm upload-file \e
    --bucket-ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --key archive/2026-08.csv --file ./2026-08.csv \e
    --part-size 8388608 --concurrency 8
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-directory (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1),
